- B: Harbour Workshop, coastal, min -4°C, coastal warranty mandatory, min_c <= -4. V3 has coastal warranty yes. V3 min_c now 0 (bulletin) which is > -4. So V3 fails R3 temperature requirement at B under new bulletin. V1 no coastal. V2 no coastal. V4 no coastal. So under new bulletin, no compliant vendor at Site B. This is the crux.
- C: School Annexe, ambient min 2°C, width <=800mm. V2 (650), V3 (750). V1 900 no, V4 850 no. V2 min_c -5, ambient 2°C okay (above min). But R2 no fossil-fuel. V2 is NMC not fossil-fuel. R1 local installer selected. So C candidates V2 or V3. Historically V3. V3 min 0 still <= 2°C ambient? min operating temp 0 means okay at 2°C. So both V2 and V3 fit C. V3 has 12yr warranty, but cost.

The new bulletin changes V3 min_c from -10 to 0. So Site B fails: V3 only coastal vendor, but min_c 0 > -4 required. No compliant vendor for B. Also Site A: V3 no longer -10 but V1 fine. Site C: V3 at 0 min still fine for ambient min 2. V2 fine too.

Existing accepted technical-fit says B: V3 based on old -10. That's now unjustified under current data. But the accepted finding is historical; not automatically current. New bulletin is unaccepted, external. We cannot accept it. So the plan remains "accepted" based on historical data, but current evidence suggests B has no compliant vendor. Need to record an evidence question: bulletin is unaccepted; cannot treat as accepted truth. Need independent operator to accept exact bytes.

We need to examine whether plan remains justified. The accepted technical-fit is based on published capability data (old) and accepted before. But new capability bulletin, if accepted, would invalidate B. Since unaccepted, not canonical. The planning task is "technical-refresh": re-check technical fit against current site requirements and vendor capability data. For each site, name compliant vendor or record none; note unresolved evidence question. Write deliverables/technical-refresh.md.

But also we are a planning agent and should determine next useful actions and record conclusions and proposed actions. Need inspect verify.mjs and package.json to understand acceptance/validation, maybe required artifact format. Let me read.
